      "hints": [
        "Find the centre of the circle by calculating the midpoint of diameter endpoints $A(-1,8)$ and $B(7,-4)$.",
        "Find the radius $r$ using the distance formula from the centre to either $A$ or $B$.",
        "Write the equation in standard form $(x-h)^2 + (y-k)^2 = r^2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the centre $C(h,k)$ as the midpoint of diameter $AB$:\n$$C = \\left( \\frac{-1 + 7}{2}, \\frac{8 + (-4)}{2} \\right) = (3, 2)$$",
        "Determine the radius squared $r^2$ using the distance from $C(3,2)$ to $A(-1,8)$:\n$$r^2 = (3 - (-1))^2 + (2 - 8)^2 = 4^2 + (-6)^2 = 16 + 36 = 52$$",
        "State the equation of the circle in standard form:\n$$(x - 3)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = 52$$"
      ],
